{
  "out": "{\"body\":\"\\\"Closes #66.\\\\n\\\\npi-action never set a thinking level, so pi-durable's `resolveAgent` used `state?.thinkingLevel ?? \\\\\\\"off\\\\\\\"`: every run was **off**, also with `model_reasoning: true`. This adds `thinking_level`, with pi's default `medium`.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes\\\\n\\\\n- **Input.** `thinking_level`: `off`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, or `max` (pi-ai's `ModelThinkingLevel`, which includes `max`). Any case. Empty → `medium`. An invalid value fails the run with the list of valid values. `src/index.ts` now reads the inputs inside the promise chain, so the error reaches `setFailed` instead of crashing.\\\\n- **Every run.** `Thread.open` adds `thinkingLevel` to the agent that `configureAgent` passes to `root.configure`, so a continuing thread switches to the new level.\\\\n- *",
